  "original_goal": {
    "selected_full_target": "Let \\(p\\) be any prime, \\(K\\) any field of characteristic \\(p\\), and\n\\(\\lambda\\) an integer with \\(0\\leq\\lambda<p\\).\nLet \\(V(\\lambda)\\) be the complex irreducible highest-weight\n\\(\\mathfrak{sl}_2(\\mathbb C)\\)-module of highest weight \\(\\lambda\\),\nof dimension \\(\\lambda+1\\). Its Chevalley generators satisfy\n\n\\[\n[h,x]=2x,\\qquad[h,y]=-2y,\\qquad[x,y]=h.\n\\]\n\nChoose a nonzero highest-weight vector \\(v\\) with \\(xv=0\\) and\n\\(hv=\\lambda v\\). Let \\(U_{\\mathbb Z}\\) be the integer subalgebra of\nthe universal enveloping algebra generated by all divided powers\n\\(X_r=x^r/r!\\), \\(Y_r=y^r/r!\\), for integers \\(r\\geq0\\).\nAn **admissible lattice** \\(M\\subset V(\\lambda)\\) is a free abelian\nsubgroup with an integer basis that is also a complex basis, stable under\n\\(U_{\\mathbb Z}\\). It is arbitrary, not necessarily the minimal lattice.\n\nPut \\(V(K)=M\\otimes_{\\mathbb Z}K\\). The Lie algebra\n\\(L(K)=(\\mathbb Zx+\\mathbb Zy+\\mathbb Zh)\\otimes_{\\mathbb Z}K\\)\nacts by the induced lattice operators. This is the Chevalley\n\\(\\mathfrak{sl}_2\\) construction also in characteristic 2.\nProve that \\(V(K)\\) is nonzero and every \\(K\\)-linear subspace\ninvariant under \\(x,y,h\\) is zero or all of \\(V(K)\\).\nBoth \\(\\lambda=0\\) and \\(p=2\\) are included; \\(K\\) need not be\nalgebraically closed.",
